<h2 id="conventions-section-categories" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0005">2.3</span> Categories</h2>

<p>
A category $\mathcal{C}$ consists of a set of objects and, for each pair of objects, a set of morphisms between them. In other words, it is what is called a “small” category in other texts. We will use “big” categories (categories whose objects form a proper class) as well, but only those that are listed in Categories, Remark <a href="/tag/0015" data-tag="0015">4.2.2</a>. 
</p>
